{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Mie2xLH1GCWCz1MMH5VDZi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have a complete understanding. Let me confirm the bug and plan the fix.\n\n**The bug** is in `advanceDecision` (boundary.ts:166): the walk excludes `candidates.length - 1` — only the *newest candidate group*. When a turnless singleton trails the newest closed turn, that singleton is the newest candidate (protected), so the newest **closed turn** sits at `length - 2` and becomes evictable. Evicting it lands the boundary on/past it, flipping it short — violating AC-5.3.\n\nLet me set up task tracking, then write the test first (to prove it catches the bug), then fix."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":63779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8291ef6-6126-40dc-b2d4-175e5ef5399e","uuid":"6cf5d54c-1a4a-41b9-971a-bfaebdffe1e6","request_id":"req_011CbzGzwt3jRTWGAgX6X6cy"}
