{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_012tPV1KSHgB1nqsb1emgKzv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I changed and verified.\n\n## The bug\n\nIn `advanceDecision` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts`), the eviction walk stopped at `candidates.length - 1` — it protected only the *newest candidate group*. The design intends that to be the newest closed turn, but when a turnless singleton trails the newest closed turn, **the singleton** is the newest candidate. The newest closed turn then sat one slot back and became evictable; evicting it lands the boundary on/past its last event order, flipping it short — a direct AC-5.3 violation.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe walk now scans candidates back-to-front for the **last one carrying a `turn_id`** (the newest closed turn) and stops the eviction loop before it. That protects the newest closed turn *and everything after it* (trailing turnless singletons), because the boundary lands on a group's last order — any landing at or beyond the newest closed turn would render it short. When the zone has no closed turn at all, it falls back to the original \"protect the newest group\" behavior (turnless-only degeneration). The peek-ahead target stop is unchanged.\n\nI also corrected the now-stale pseudocode in the story doc (`stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md`), which still read \"excluding newest group always\" — it now matches the grouping-rules table and the code.\n\n## Test coverage (TC-5.2)\n\nAdded a test in `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`: turns 50/45 then a trailing turnless 70 (total 165 > max 100). The newest closed turn (45) and trailing turnless (70) are both protected; only t1 (50) evicts, boundary lands on t1, zone legally stays at 115. It asserts no partial-turn flip, that t1 is the only abridged result, and that both the newest closed turn and the trailing turnless render full.\n\nI confirmed it's a meaningful test: **against the unfixed code it failed** (boundary advanced to position 7 — the newest closed turn — instead of 3), and it passes after the fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused boundary tests: `view-boundary.test.ts` + `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` → **20 passed**.\n- Configured story gate: `red-verify` (build, typecheck, lint, boundaries — all OK) + the two focused files → **green**.\n- Re-recorded the `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` hash in `test/red-manifest.json` (per the story DoD); immutability check passes (51 files unchanged). The manifest's large `git diff` is pre-existing working-tree state — my command changed only the one intended line.\n\nOne note: I left the manifest update as the single-line hash change for the amended test; the rest of that file's diff predates this task."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":90115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8291ef6-6126-40dc-b2d4-175e5ef5399e","uuid":"b5f28132-780a-4969-ae5f-07c8c5348fdc","request_id":"req_011CbzHK7FrgCAPj3R7pxJb7"}
